  "source": "one-continuous-master",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "line-01",
      "text": "The Blue Fairy noticed Pinocchio hanging helplessly from the giant oak.",
      "start": 0.15,
      "end": 5.14
    },
    {
      "id": "line-02",
      "text": "She sent a Falcon to cut the rope and rescue him.",
      "start": 5.14,
      "end": 8.431
    },
    {
      "id": "line-03",
      "text": "Her elegant Poodle carried the puppet home in a tiny carriage.",
      "start": 8.431,
      "end": 12.991
    },
    {
      "id": "line-04",
      "text": "A Crow, Owl, and Talking Cricket debated whether their patient was alive.",
      "start": 12.991,
      "end": 19.757
    },
    {
      "id": "line-05",
      "text": "Pinocchio refused the bitter medicine until Black Rabbits arrived for him.",
      "start": 19.757,
      "end": 25.326
    },
    {
      "id": "line-06",
      "text": "He swallowed it immediately and recovered from his dangerous fever.",
      "start": 25.326,
      "end": 30.56
    },
    {
      "id": "line-07",
      "text": "When the Fairy asked about the coins, Pinocchio invented several lies.",
      "start": 30.56,
      "end": 35.65
    },
    {
      "id": "line-08",
      "text": "His nose lengthened after every false answer until he could barely move.",
      "start": 35.65,
      "end": 41.952
    },
    {
      "id": "line-09",
      "text": "The Fairy forgave him and called Woodpeckers to shorten the nose.",
      "start": 41.952,
      "end": 46.464
    },
    {
      "id": "line-10",
      "text": "She promised that Geppetto could soon join them as a family.",
      "start": 46.464,
      "end": 51.126
    },
    {
      "id": "line-11",
      "text": "On the way to meet his father, Pinocchio met the Fox and Cat again.",
      "start": 51.126,
      "end": 55.904
    },
    {
      "id": "line-12",
      "text": "Ignoring experience, he followed them toward the Field of Wonders.",
      "start": 55.904,
      "end": 61.377
    },
    {
      "id": "line-13",
      "text": "He buried his four coins and waited for a tree of money.",
      "start": 61.377,
      "end": 65.817
    },
    {
      "id": "line-14",
      "text": "A laughing Parrot revealed that the swindlers had stolen everything.",
      "start": 65.817,
      "end": 71.609
    },
    {
      "id": "line-15",
      "text": "The local judge listened to the robbery, then imprisoned the victim.",
      "start": 71.609,
      "end": 76.321
    },
    {
      "id": "line-16",
      "text": "Only a royal celebration freed Pinocchio four months later.",
      "start": 76.321,
      "end": 82.181
    }
  ],
